atlas optimization-cheap-cognition

architecture cheap-cognition
  canonical_name CheapCognition
  owns CognitiveMicroRoute
  owns AdmissibleRole
  consumes ExactMask
  consumes CandidateSet
  consumes InformationPolicy
  publishes CandidateClassification
  publishes EscalationDecision
  family optimization
  domain Optimization / Cognitive control plane
  layer execution
  semantic_question Is this decision a classification a tiny local model can make inside an exact mask, or does it require an expensive operator?
  purpose Give the machine a cheap semantic control plane that removes expensive cognition from paths that never needed it, without letting an approximate operator take a decision that must be exact.
  maturity implemented
  source_path components/BonfyreDecision/channel-yield.mjs
  source_path components/BonfyreDecision/decision-plane.cue
  source_path cmd/BonfyreSourceFrontier/tools/qualify_channels.mjs
  source_path scripts/qualify_continuously.sh
  source_path cmd/BonfyreDecide/src/dp_gguf.c
  witness components/BonfyreDecision/tests/channel-yield.test.mjs proves the ordered replay never shows a record an outcome recorded after it, training is byte-deterministic, a shadow assessment is a validated DecisionPlane receipt bound to the weight file's SHA-256, and skip value is computed by assessSelectiveValue against timed qualifier outcomes
  witness components/BonfyreDecision/results/channel-yield-offline-20261016.json trains weights cb5713ef (frozen for the live holdout) on the first 73,854 of 92,318 ordered qualifier outcomes and replays the last 18,464: Brier 0.052 against 0.077 for the base rate; worked in score order, 50% of yields arrive in the first 10% of observations against 9.5% as run, 76% in the first quarter against 23%, 94% in the first half against 44%; skipping below 0.01 drops 26% of observations and loses 3.9% of yields
  witness cmd/BonfyreDecide/tests/parity.sh exercises the C owner (dp_gguf.c) against tests/mock_front.c: forced-continuation scoring over a token trie for an 18-account chart, lettered questions asked in both orders with the content-free prior, checkpoint pinning and a lease granted and released, byte-identical to the retired Bun owner (2026-10-22)
  known_gap the refusal paths ported into dp_gguf.c (an unreported option token, option names that extend one another, a letter read as zero over a non-negligible tail) were proven on the retired Bun owner and are not yet exercised by a C vector
  invariant the first admitted role is SourceFrontier channel_qualification: before an observation is spent, the DecisionPlane gives the probability that it yields a qualifying channel or a page that declares channels, from the address and the publisher's earlier outcomes only
  invariant the owner is a pinned local logistic weight file trained on the qualifier's own ordered evidence; the qualifier still observes every claimed candidate and owns admission
  invariant receipts are written before the qualifier observes the same slice, so its timed outcomes are an independent holdout for the frozen weights; the gate stays SHADOW until assessSelectiveValue on that holdout is promotion-eligible
  forbidden_inference yields found earlier in an ordered replay -> sources admitted sooner in the live chain; ordering reaches WorkGraph priority only with BONFYRE_QUALIFY_ORDER=yield, off by default
  forbidden_inference a skipped observation that would have refused -> a worthless channel; a refusal is how one fetch ended on one day
  known_gap the live holdout has no timed outcomes yet: qualify_channels began recording observe_ms and channel_id on 2026-10-16
  known_gap Clef, the pinned DecisionPlane owner, took 32 to 132 s per assessment on this machine's CPU (tests/trained-runtime-witness.json), longer than the observations it would avoid; it is not the owner here
  node_types CheapClassifier
  node_types AdmissibleRole
  node_types InadmissibleRole
  node_types EscalationBoundary
  edge_types classifies
  edge_types escalates_to
  edge_types bounded_by
  invariant a cheap classifier runs inside an exact mask over a bounded candidate set, never over an open world
  invariant a cheap classifier proposes; the exact layer disposes
  invariant no authority, permission, effect admission or proof outcome is ever decided by an approximate operator
  invariant a classification carries its confidence and its escalation path; an unresolved case escalates rather than guesses
  invariant the cheap stage is measured by how much expensive cognition it avoided, not by its own accuracy alone
  invariant a cheap classifier may discover a compression opportunity; only the exact layer may act on one
  invariant a local GGUF owner gives probability only to what the server scored: up to five options are lettered and asked in both orders; more are scored as forced continuations of each option name, one call per distinct token prefix; an option token the server did not report refuses the answer, and mass said off the list is abstention (none) rather than spread over unscored options
  invariant a GGUF answer is bound to the checkpoint by SHA-256, device, inode, size and nanosecond modification and change times and to the model the server names on every call; the batch holds the model by a front lease
  invariant the checkpoint is hashed through one descriptor whose identity must hold from open to close; its digest is kept per process (16 files) and as one row per path in ~/.bonfyre/state/checkpoints.sqlite, replaced when the file's identity changes; the JSON sidecar is no longer read or written and the model directory is never written
  invariant a lease reply must name the lease it answers (renewed/released true); a grant is released when owner start-up fails after it; a refused or malformed grant is an error, and only 404 (plain llama-server) means unleased; an unacknowledged release keeps the lease for retry
  invariant templates, option tokens and calibration priors share a 128-entry, 1 MiB serialized-payload memo per owner, and coverage keeps the latest 128 readings
  witness cmd/BonfyreDecide/tests/parity.sh runs every model-assisted vector with a fresh BONFYRE_HOME, so the C owner writes the checkpoint row in state/checkpoints.sqlite (shared with the Bun schema) and takes and releases a front lease each run (2026-10-22)
  known_gap rehash on a changed checkpoint, a refused grant, release after a failed start-up and an unacknowledged release kept for retry are ported into dp_gguf.c but were witnessed only on the retired Bun owner (2026-10-17)
  forbidden_inference the memo budget -> the owner's memory; it bounds serialized payload, not process memory, and a lost grant reply with no lease id still relies on the front's ttl
  forbidden_inference a cheap classification -> a resolved finding
  forbidden_inference a cheap classification -> a granted authority
  forbidden_inference high classifier confidence -> exactness
  forbidden_inference a cheap stage being available -> it being cheaper than a bitmap intersection
  forbidden_inference a named option the model generated -> a distribution over the declared options; only scored options carry probability
  interacts optimization-cascade
  interacts compression-law
  source_lineage Generation-10 optimization doctrine promotion, 2026-08-26

admissible_role assign a repair phenotype to a finding before expensive analysis
admissible_role propose a likely duplicate family
admissible_role propose a business-impact class
admissible_role propose a likely proof family
admissible_role estimate escalation likelihood
admissible_role assign a route or function to a candidate capability family
admissible_role assign a motif to a candidate domain operation
admissible_role tokenize a scraped title into candidate entity attributes
admissible_role classify a phrase as carrying a candidate contract term
admissible_role triage a new failure as known phenotype, provider-shaped, carrier-shaped, contract-shaped or new
admissible_role separate likely reusable motifs from incidental similarity before expensive analysis

inadmissible_role deciding that a security finding is resolved
inadmissible_role granting or denying authority
inadmissible_role admitting an effect
inadmissible_role establishing entity identity as fact
inadmissible_role closing a proof obligation
inadmissible_role deciding what a downstream estate may see

escalation_boundary exact-rule
  detail The classification maps onto a deterministic rule that resolves the case exactly.
escalation_boundary latent-search
  detail The classification narrows to a neighborhood that similarity search can rank.
escalation_boundary deeper-model
  detail The case is genuinely ambiguous and warrants an expensive operator over a small residue.

ordering_note the measured best order varies by subject family; exact then latent then cheap-model is sometimes cheaper than exact then cheap-model then latent, and the planner selects on measurement rather than doctrine
discovery_note the highest-value use of this stage is separating reusable structure from incidental similarity across a very large candidate population, which makes cheap cognition a producer of compression opportunities and not only a consumer of them
